  The research                                                           │ ⢀⠔⠁⠔⠊⠉       ⢸
                                                                      0% │⡠⠃⠉           ⢸                    sets/week
  A 2025 meta-regression of resistance-training studies modelled         └────────────────────────────────────────────
  muscle growth against weekly sets per muscle. Growth keeps             0                10         20             30
  rising with volume, but each extra set adds less: the curve         faint lines: 95% credible interval
  flattens past roughly 12 sets a week.

  PureSets is inspired by this research, not trying to prescribe.
  Pick a target you can sustain and recover from.

  Source  https://link.springer.com/10.1007/s40279-025-02344-w

  How logging works

  1  Press enter on Home (or a to search everything).
  2  Type to find the exercise you did.
  3  Press enter, then choose how many hard sets.
  4  Press enter to log. Every muscle it works is credited.
  5  Check Home for what still needs work this week.

  Primary movers get one set per set performed. Secondary movers
  get half, because they help but are not the main target.
